{
  "id": "finite-source-machine-repair-sixth-control",
  "name": "Finite-source machine repair with a shared repairer",
  "description": "Original four-state probability model for three identical machines sharing one repairer. Each operating machine fails independently at exponential rate Failure_Rate; one busy repairer completes repairs at exponential rate Repair_Rate. Probability stocks describe an ensemble distribution, not a sampled failure path or a continuous number of broken machines. Three-machine topology is fixed: changing population requires rebuilding states, not editing a population parameter. Nonnegative rates and probability initial conditions summing to one. No spares, common-cause failures, aging, travel time, repairer vacations or empirical calibration. Defaults illustrative. Coarse numerical steps can violate probability positivity; no clipping or renormalization.",
  "category": "engineering",
  "source": "https://www.kent.ac.uk/smsas/personal/lb209/files/sp14.pdf",
  "reference": "Lothar Breuer, Introduction to Stochastic Processes, section3.3.6 printed pp53-54, finite-source transition rates and machine-repair interpretation. Original JSON/equation implementation, no source text/code/figures copied.",
